## API-First Development

### Overview

All API development follows an **API-First** approach where the OpenAPI specification serves as the single source of truth for API contracts between frontend and backend teams.

### Development Workflow

When implementing any new feature or API endpoint, follow this enhanced workflow:

1. **🎯 Task Assignment** - Understand requirements and scope
2. **📋 API Design** - Create/update OpenAPI specification in `api-spec/` project
3. **⚙️ Code Generation** - Generate FastAPI controllers and TypeScript clients
4. **🔧 Backend Implementation** - Implement business logic in services layer
5. **🎨 Frontend Implementation** - Build UI components using generated clients
6. **🧪 E2E Testing** - Validate complete workflow with Cypress
7. **📖 Documentation** - Update PROJECT_PLAN.md and mark task completed
8. **🔍 Quality Review** - Ensure all standards are followed
9. **✅ Regression Testing** - Validate all existing functionality still works

### Project Structure with OpenAPI

```
book-course-converter/
├── api-spec/                    # Separate OpenAPI project
│   ├── openapi/
│   │   ├── schemas/            # Reusable schemas
│   │   │   ├── book.yaml
│   │   │   ├── course.yaml
│   │   │   └── common.yaml
│   │   ├── paths/              # API endpoints
│   │   │   ├── books/
│   │   │   │   ├── upload.yaml
│   │   │   │   ├── list.yaml
│   │   │   │   └── get.yaml
│   │   │   └── courses/
│   │   ├── spec.yaml           # Main OpenAPI spec
│   │   └── package.json        # Generation scripts
│   ├── generated/              # Generated code output
│   │   ├── python/            # FastAPI models & routes
│   │   └── typescript/        # Axios clients & types
│   └── scripts/               # Code generation scripts
├── backend/                    # FastAPI backend
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── services/          # Business logic implementation
│   │   └── main.py
└── frontend/                   # React frontend
    ├── src/
    │   └── features/
```

- Frontend and backend should import openapi generated artifacts directly.
- Backend and frontend must not contain tests theirselves. Only e2e testing is allowed in separate project

### Testing Strategy

- **Full Stack Testing**: Backend and frontend running together
- **Real User Scenarios**: Test actual user workflows
- **API Contract Validation**: Ensure frontend and backend communicate correctly
- **Data Persistence**: Verify data flows through the entire system
- **Error Handling**: Test error scenarios and edge cases
